  "decisions": {
    "D-06": "A physics arm never halts on invariant B or any other causal-front rule. At the budget-rule readings it logs the frozen monitor's per-bin causal weights and front. It does not run a live 256-identity monitor every step. Phase 61 builds the observe-only guard.",
    "D-07": "If the owner continues at checkpoint 4, R_ref is re-measured and GATE-04 is re-run at the approved first_omega_0 before any physics arm. Neither step trains. GATE-04 is the complete-pass rule of 57-RULING.md (GAP-56-01). A fail stops for the owner.",
    "D-08": "Probe physics arms reuse the Stage-0 R_ref in force and do not re-measure it. The run record says the value is the Stage-0 reference applied unchanged.",
    "D-09": "The Phase 59 verifier accepts exactly one successor SHA-256 for pinn/verification/feasibility_scorer.py, named in the committed scorer-successor.json. Every other producer hash is still checked against the Phase 59 result files.",
    "D-10": "Both scored states of every real arm are committed in plain git, not Git LFS. Resume checkpoints and timing-run weights stay out of git. Re-deriving a result re-scores the committed weights.",
    "D-11": "A continue-path arm is legal only when a committed ruling file quotes the owner's message and names the approved first_omega_0. Every continue-path arm record cites it. A physics arm refuses any other value."
  },
